rop the @CK."],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["up","40"],["hs","wd"],["nt","\nThe only problem with this plan is that West is very likely to have 6 diamonds. "],["pg",""],["hs","es"],["at","If allowed to win trick 1, West will be able to give East a diamond ruff."],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["ls","es"],["hs","sd"],["nt","\nSouth should win the opening lead "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","da"],["pg",""],["at","and play his winners as before with the intention of ^*Bstrip squeezing^*N West."],["pg",""],["tc","c"],["pc","!hk"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!sa"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!sk"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!sq"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!sj"],["pc","!d"],["pc","!s"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!st"],["pc","!d"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!s9"],["pc","!d"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!h"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!ha"],["pc","!h"],["tc","r"],["hs","nh"],["nt","\nOn dummy's last heart, "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","d"],["hs","wd"],["at","West must discard a diamond in order to guard the @CK. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","nd"],["at","A diamond trick is now conceded to West "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["pc","d"],["pc","c"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","sc"],["at","forcing him to lead into South's club tenace. There may be ambiguity in the ending and South will likely have to guess West's remaining distribution."],["pg",""],["up","5"],["ls","sc"],["hs","wd"],["nt","\nThe ^*B2-suit strip squeeze^*N is quite common. In this case, West was squeezed out of a surplus winner in diamonds so that he could be endplayed without being able to set the contract. This particular variety of strip squeeze matures with 2 or more losers."],["",""]]}}